FUNCTION CALLC.EXISTS(FNAME)
* mv_package — core capability probe for UniData.  GPL-2.0-only.
*
* CALLC.EXISTS(name) — 1 if the CallC function `name` is registered with
* this UniData, else 0, WITHOUT invoking it.  A CallC to an unregistered
* function aborts the whole program (no trappable error), so a live probe
* is impossible; this reads the canonical CallC definition the package
* manager maintains ($UDTHOME/bin/work/cfuncdef).
*
* This is the answer to "is an optional native add-on installed?" that does
* NOT require the add-on — or even a specific package — to be present.  The
* package manager catalogs it GLOBALLY (udt/setup.sh), so every account can
* ask before using a capability and run either way:
*
*    DEFFUN CALLC.EXISTS(A)
*    IF CALLC.EXISTS("CURSINIT") THEN
*       GOSUB FULL.SCREEN.UI        ;* udt_curses is installed — use it
*    END ELSE
*       GOSUB PLAIN.UI             ;* runs on a bare account too
*    END
*
* The program compiles and runs whether or not the capability is installed:
* only CALLC.EXISTS itself must be present, and it always is.
   FOUND = 0
   UDT = GETENV("UDTHOME")
   IF UDT # "" THEN
      OSREAD DEF FROM UDT : "/bin/work/cfuncdef" ELSE DEF = ""
      NL = DCOUNT(DEF, CHAR(10))
      I = 1
      LOOP WHILE I <= NL AND FOUND = 0 DO
         IF FIELD(FIELD(DEF, CHAR(10), I), ":", 1) = FNAME THEN FOUND = 1
         I = I + 1
      REPEAT
   END
   RETURN FOUND
